{
  "id": "remove-element",
  "questionId": "remove-element",
  "slug": "remove-element",
  "title": "Remove Element",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Two pointers",
  "patterns": [
    "two pointers",
    "in-place filtering"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "you don't need to shift every remaining element one at a time - what if you tracked where the next kept element should go?",
    "walk through the array with a read pointer; whenever the current value isn't val, place it at a separate write pointer position and advance the write pointer",
    "the write pointer only moves when you keep something, so it naturally compacts the array as you go",
    "at the end, everything before the write pointer is your answer, everything after can be discarded or ignored"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "removing elements from the middle of an array one at a time, which shifts everything after it and costs O(n) per removal",
    "comparing against the wrong variable, e.g. filtering by index instead of by value",
    "not preserving the original relative order of the kept elements",
    "confusing this with 'remove duplicates', which is a different problem - here you remove one specific value, not repeats"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of integers and a target value.\n\n**Remove every occurrence of that value from the list, keeping the remaining elements in their original relative order, and return the list that's left.**\n\nThe classic in-place version of this problem also cares about not using extra space and reporting a count, but for this exercise just return the resulting list directly.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= nums.length <= 100",
      "0 <= nums[i] <= 50",
      "0 <= val <= 100",
      "val may not appear in nums at all"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "an empty input list",
      "every element equals val (result is empty)",
      "no element equals val (result is unchanged)",
      "val appears at the very first and very last positions"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [3,2,2,3], val = 3",
        "output": "[2,2]",
        "expectedOutput": "[2,2]",
        "explanation": "both 3s are removed, leaving the two 2s in their original order"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [0,1,2,2,3,0,4,2], val = 2",
        "output": "[0,1,3,0,4]",
        "expectedOutput": "[0,1,3,0,4]",
        "explanation": "every 2 is removed; everything else keeps its relative order"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1,2,3,4], val = 5",
        "output": "[1,2,3,4]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1,2,3,4]",
        "explanation": "val never appears, so nothing is removed"
      }
